# Force LF line endings in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF -> CRLF on
# checkout. A .sbatch file with CRLF fails on the Phoenix compute nodes with a
# confusing "$'\r': command not found". Without this file, every Windows user
# who clones the repo would silently receive broken job scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces: these must never be CRLF, whatever the auto-detection decides.
*.sbatch text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
